      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "component_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-114159 (GHSA-3cgx-w6gm-fqrx) is a .NET remote code execution issue: an oversized Portable PDB document name can be truncated during allocation and cause a heap out-of-bounds write in Microsoft.DiaSymReader.Native, the native Windows PDB reader bundled with .NET on Windows. Microsoft lists only Windows (x86, x64 and Arm64) as affected: .NET installed on Windows and the Microsoft.NETCore.App.Runtime.win-* runtime packs, fixed in .NET 8.0.34 (https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/security/advisories/GHSA-3cgx-w6gm-fqrx, https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/521). DHI dotnet8-runtime for Alpine 3.23 builds .NET 8 for Linux from Microsoft's source release, and each build's version is the .NET runtime version it carries; 8.0.34-r0 is built from the dotnet/dotnet v8.0.134 source tag (https://github.com/dotnet/dotnet/releases/tag/v8.0.134). Scanned all 220 packages of the ten published builds (8.0.23-r0, 8.0.24-r0, 8.0.25-r0, 8.0.26-r0, 8.0.27-r0, 8.0.29-r0, 8.0.31-r0, 8.0.32-r0, 8.0.33-r0 and 8.0.34-r0) for x86_64 and aarch64, including the files inside the nupkg and other zip archives they hold: none of them contains a Microsoft.DiaSymReader.Native file, none of them contains a native Windows PE file or a Mach-O file, and every PE file in them is a managed .NET assembly with a CLR header. They do carry Microsoft.DiaSymReader.dll, a managed .NET assembly, in the .NET SDK held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap and as NuGet packages in dotnet8-runtime-artifacts; the advisory does not list that package."
